r the Obama  administration - but since Donald Trump  became president undocumented immigrants  in the US are more frightened about  their future  [Music]  working as a truck mechanic is usually  considered a man's job in most places in  the world but in India one woman is  challenging the stereotype  [Music]  shanti devi at work she replaces truck  tires checks them for wear and tear and  fixes flats in a sari and bangle  she's an unusual figure in sanjay gandhi  transport another a huge trucking hub in  not Delhi an estimated 20,000 trucks  rolled by every day thousands more are  parked here for repairs and refueling  Shanti Devi and her husband set up a tea  shop here 20 years ago they expanded the  business to start a tire of their  workshop  the shop is hard work the to put in at  least 10 hours every day sometimes more  the tyres weigh at least 50 kilos and  have to be moved around the shop has no  toilet and no electricity connection  look that's an old tire it's travelled  thousands of kilometres through slush  and mud and God knows what else you have  to be prepared to get your hands dirty  it's a tough job hard work is something  the 55 year old is used to she grew up  in poverty in the central Indian state  of Madhya Pradesh working all her life  as a seamstress and in a cigarette  factory to make ends meet her husband  ram bahadur says he initially had doubts  about his wife working with him in a  trucking center but she's crude to metal  it's a man strong but he who had a woman  who is doing a man's job  but her presence in an environment  heavily dominated by men  still raises eyebrows here I've  travelled a lot in my life and I've  never seen anything like this a woman  working as a truck mechanic and really  amazed I don't think this work is  you need a lot of strength for this you  have to change tires pickin boots men  are more knowledgeable bugs but muhammad  islam who was hired as a mechanic by  shanti devi disagrees I have no problem  working we worked together as a team  Shanti and a husband make around four  hundred and seventy euros a month  they saved enough to build a house which  they share with the children and the  families though Shanti Devi herself was  unable to bear school she's determined  that her granddaughters get a good  education earlier people used to say why  educate a girl she's going to get  married anyway  and will stay at home but that's wrong  it's important for women not to stand on  her own feet so that she can feed  herself and her children Shanti Devi is  now urging her daughters-in-law  to learn sewing and get some part-time  work she's very inspiring you realize  that women can do any job and they're  equal to men Shanti Devi hopes her story  will embolden other women to break  barriers  years of austerity in Greece have led to  unemployment poverty and hardship for  many now the crisis is also affecting  the country's once affluent professional  classes  [Music]  it doesn't matter how loudly they  advertise their wares or how busy it is  there's hardly anyone buying anything at  column areas weekly market let alone the  more expensive products like fish and  exotic fruits and veg and that's  although the town is relatively well-off  there are high earners here  entrepreneurs freelancers Callum area is  home to northern Greece's upper middle  class like gallery owner Marta varruchi  till 2012 was very good for me but then  I realized that the situation is going  down and I decided to close the store  that was the only way she could avoid  bankruptcy today she relies on food  donations from the local welfare center  her savings are long gone and she gets  no state support  I lost my pride my life was perfect  now now it's nothing and she's not alone  the vicious circle of banking crisis tax  hikes and government austerity measures  is ruining Greece's middle class  Constantino gugus was a successful  architect now he finds he often can't  afford to pay his electricity bill if 